{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794258779,"nonce":"Xi1Mra5nSs8yIB6FQGmfsMhJQ1Q=","title":"Overlay, subtree and Stateful-refresh builds have no owner, so what they create is never disposed","message":"From the allocation audit (code read; growth not observed in a running app).\n\nOnly full rebuilds run inside `BuildScope::begin` (blinc_app windowed/event_loop/frame/rebuild.rs). Overlay builds (rebuild.rs overlay paths), `refresh_stateful` / `check_stateful_deps`, and DSL `with`-region re-renders (blinc_dsl_core with_regions.rs) run outside any `Owner`. In blinc_layout only region.rs uses `Owner`.\n\nSo every computed / effect / signal a widget creates while built there is never disposed, and the effects keep running on every write. cn widgets create several during build (color_picker effects, select, calendar, resizable, navigation_menu, media). Each DSL `computed{}` style argument (blinc_dsl_core host.rs) adds a derived per re-render. Grows per overlay open and per subtree rebuild.\n\nAlso: closing a secondary window (windowed event_loop.rs) drops its `BuildScope`, and neither `BuildScope` nor `Owner` implements `Drop`, so that window's effects and computeds are never disposed.\n\nFollow-up to 9fee179 (full rebuilds), which also noted that desktop `BuildScope::keep` holds every incremental build's owner until the next fresh tree.","files":null}]}